Z||000000||filthyscarecrow||12-02-2001||08:35 PM||||here are the pics of my tails. they cost about $10 to make.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierotails2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierotails1.jpg"> <P>they're not sequential or anything. they're jsut the fluorescent light lens painted with testors transparent candy red on the back. they are held in place with a putty like substance, and everything around them is painted black. they're very easy to do, and i think they look a lot cooler than stock... ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tabs31||12-02-2001||08:53 PM||||WOW!!!!!!!!! That looks great!!!!! you have any pics of you making them??<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tabs31_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||filthyscarecrow||12-02-2001||09:10 PM||||no, unfortunately. but i do still have the patterns for the lenses. they're really easy. <BR>yuo'll need:<BR>1 can transparent red paint ($3 at walmart)<BR>i sheet of fluorescent light lens ($6, Home depot)<BR>tape<BR>access to a disc sander<BR>flat black bottle paint<BR>just cut out the lenses the right shape (i can make jpeg files of the lenses to email those who are interested)<BR>paint them red on the pointy side (all except for the backup lights)<BR>mask off circles on the flat side and paint the outsides of them black.<BR>take the tails apart (be really careful, they're old, they'll crack easily)<BR>take out the old red and white lenses and replace them with the new lenses and use the shoe goo/putty stuff to hold them in place. then just paint everything outside the lenses flat black. <BR>put them back together and put em back on the car. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||12-02-2001||09:11 PM||||I don't think the red paint will hold up thru the seasons... How about this... Instead of painting them... Buy a roll of that taillight repair vinyl tape (sold at all auto stores) & put that on the lens... The tape is even colored, translucent & should last a very long time... Just an idea...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I'm sure for most of us this will work for off road only.... but what the hell, as long as the police don't pull me over..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>P.S. Good work...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">      <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">1984 Indy For Sale ~ <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000004||filthyscarecrow||12-02-2001||09:50 PM||||i was thinkin about the tape too haze. it's not a bad idea at all, but i only drive my car during the summer, so i'm not too worried about it, and the lenses aren't glued in, so i can always repaint them. maybe i'll do the tape next time...||||reg||1
